articleSummary:
Ebola outbreak in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo remains ongoing as of June 2026. Since the May 15 declaration, 75 healthcare workers have contracted Ebola and 17 have died, per WHO Emergency Director Marie Roseline Belizaire. Nearly 900 confirmed cases and 232 deaths have been reported across 33 health zones in three provinces: Ituri, North Kivu, and South Kivu, with Ituri accounting for about 95% of cases. About 90% of patients initially did not show hemorrhagic symptoms, leading many to self-medicate at home or seek traditional healers. Community resistance complicates containment, and authorities warn the health system is stretched with insufficient staff. The response emphasizes rapid case detection, free treatment, and risk communication to mobilize community collaboration. Health Minister Roger Kamba visited Bunia Hospital in Ituri to commend frontline doctors and nurses.”} }` } }?Oops repeated. The correct JSON should be single object with summary string. Ensure formatting. The extra trailing characters should be removed. Let's provide clean.  Wait the previous included stray characters at end. Let's deliver clean.  

